  "report_period": "Week 30 (18th Jul to 25th Jul 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Sinokor Maritime have committed the Capesize \"Pacific West\" 175/2012 Jinhai, China (SS 11/2027, DD 03/2026, Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 27,1 mill. Remind you that the \"Pacific South\" 176/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS 06/2027, DD 09/2025) was committed a couple of weeks ago at excess USD 27 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Ultra Lion\" 81/2015 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 01/2030, DD 01/2028, Scrubber fitted) was committed at USD 24,8 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger \"Ultra Puma\" 81/2016 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 08/2026) was sold a week ago at USD 25,3 mill. Grace Ocean have committed their Ultramax \"Nord Kitan\" 60/2017 Saiki, Japan (SS/DD 01/2027) to undisclosed interests at USD 24 mill. Note that earlier in July, the \"IVS Swinley Forest\" 60/2017 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 01/2027) was sold at USD 23,3 mill. On the Supramax sector, following the sale of the \"Jin Gang\" 56/2009 Chengxi, China (SS 04/2029, DD 06/2027) at USD 10,8 mill, clients of Jinhui Shipping have committed the sister vessel \"Jin Ji\" 56/2009 Chengxi, China (SS 09/2029, DD 09/2026) at USD 11 mill. Furthermore, the \"Epic Trader\" 56/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS 08/2027, DD 10/2025) of Load Line Marine was committed to Chinese interests at xs USD 13 mill. Remind you that back in May, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Minoas\" 56/2011 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 04/2026) was sold at USD 11,8 mill. Island View Shipping have committed their OHBS Handysize \"IVS Kinglet\" 33/2011 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 08/2026) at USD 12,25 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Maple Tulip\" 33/2011 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 10/2025, OHBS) was sold back in May at USD 11,8 mill.",
    "tankers": "Kazmortransflot have acquired the Aframax sisters \"Dune\" & \"Lamu\" 113/2025 Cosco, China (SS 06/2030, DD 06/2028 & SS 05/2030, DD 05/2028, Scrubber fitted, Ice Class 1C) at USD 72 mill each. Note that the \"Hesperia Tide\" 115/2025 Zhoushan, China (SS 01/2030, DD 03/2028, Scrubber fitted) was committed a week ago at USD 71 mill. The MR2 \"Oriental Diamond\" & \"Oriental Gold\" 50/2008 Spp, Korea (SS 04/2028, DD 05/2026 & SS 06/2028, DD 07/2026) of HMM were committed to Greek interests at USD 15,5 mill each. For reference, the sister vessel \"Valrossa\" 50/2008 Spp, Korea (SS 03/2028, DD 05/2026) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 17 mill. Zacchello Group have committed the MR1 \"Favola\" 37/2002 Stx, Korea (SS 08/2027, DD 11/2025) to Nigerian interests at xs USD 7 mill. Remind you that back in May, same owners committed the sister vessel \"Zagara\" 37/2002 Stx, Korea (SS 04/2027, DD 07/2025) at USD 8 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 13,000/15,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/17,000 pd. Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 15,000/18,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 30,000/32,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 26,000/28,000 pd. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 15,500 pd for 12/14 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/17,000 pd. West coast Indian trips via Arabian Gulf into India were fixed around usd 12,000/13,000 pd. West coast Indian trips via South Africa into East Coast india were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. South African trips into South East Asia were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 140K/150K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "West African trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 12,000/13,000 pd. Continental trips into US Gulf were fixed around usd 8,000/10,000 pd. Inter-Mediterranean trips via Black Sea were reported at the level of usd 6,000/8,000 pd. US Gulf trips into North Coast South America-Caribbean range were fixed around usd 15,000/16,000 pd. North Coast South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 16,000/17,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
